# Rust
# Cargo.lock IS committed. contracts/ builds programs, not a library, and the
# Solana toolchain bundles an old cargo (1.84 for solana 2.3.0) that cannot
# parse edition2024 manifests. Without a lock, cargo re-resolves to whatever
# is newest and `anchor build` breaks on a different crate each time.
**/*.rs.bk

# Signer keyshares (NEVER commit these)
keyshare*.json
!keyshare.example.json

